WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:01.390
- Y'all, let's finish up with something

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:03.420
we came across on social media.

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:04.803
This is "What I'm liking."

00:00:04.803 --> 00:00:07.380
(upbeat drum music)

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:10.140
An attorney turned pasta maker.

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:11.490
That's right, that's what I said.

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:14.100
Is sharing his secrets to
creating some of the most

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:16.290
colorful and interesting noodles ever.

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:18.240
He makes everything from ravioli

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:21.660
to lasagna soup, all from scratch. I know.

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:24.360
Check out TikTok's Danny Loves Pasta.

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:25.890
- [Danny] Last year,
my lasagna soup videos

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:27.750
got almost a hundred million views

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:29.400
and now that the weather
is getting colder,

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:30.420
it's time to bring it back.

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:33.060
Lasagna soup is basically
a deconstructed lasagna.

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:36.275
And if you remember, we call
this the sizzle lasagna soup.

00:00:36.275 --> 00:00:37.949
(audience applauds)

00:00:37.949 --> 00:00:39.660
- My mouth is watering.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:43.770
That post combined got over
a hundred million views,

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:46.170
so people are into lasagna soup

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:47.280
is what we have figured out.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:50.340
Now Danny has a book out
called "Danny Loves Pasta,"

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:53.130
and we have him on the line
watching on NBC New York.

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:55.004
What's up Danny?
(audience applauds)

00:00:55.004 --> 00:00:57.180
- Hi Kelly, thanks for having me.

00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:59.010
- Well, thank you for joining us.

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:03.963
So how does one go from
lawyer to pasta expert?

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:07.440
- Well, pasta has always
been my favorite food,

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:08.760
and when I was growing up,

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:11.970
my grandmother was this
amazing Italian American cook

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:13.620
and she would make these huge feasts,

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:15.630
and I'm kind of embarrassed to say this,

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:17.010
but I was a very picky eater,

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.590
so I would always only eat
the pasta she would make.

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:22.170
And she would always make
fresh pasta for Christmas.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.360
So in 2020, my husband and I

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:25.560
had just had a newborn baby,

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:26.970
so we couldn't go home for Christmas.

00:01:26.970 --> 00:01:29.400
So I was like, "I'm gonna
learn how to make fresh pasta."

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:33.030
I made her fresh pasta. I
called her, she loved it.

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:35.580
But unfortunately,
shortly after Christmas,

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:39.060
my grandmother very
unexpectedly passed away

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:40.410
and it was very, very hard on me.

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:42.093
I had been so close with her,

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:45.750
so I just kept making
pasta in her memory to try

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:49.410
and keep her memory alive
and to feel close with her.

00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:53.100
And it kind of just snowballed
from there very unexpectedly.

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:54.420
- Oh, that's so beautiful.

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:56.130
So how did you get so good at it?

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:57.213
Just practice?

00:01:58.590 --> 00:01:59.880
- Practice, practice, practice.

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:02.280
I started with her
recipes, and then I sort of

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:03.660
took it in a different direction.

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:06.870
I use all natural ingredients
like spinach and beets

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:11.310
and turmeric to make a pasta
in every color of the rainbow.

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:12.720
Now we have a 3-year-old daughter

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:13.890
and a three-month-old daughter.

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:16.500
So my older daughter likes
to be in the kitchen with me,

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:17.910
so I'm always making shapes for her.

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:20.520
I make cute pasta that
looks like her favorite

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:22.500
cartoon characters or flowers

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:24.420
or plants or unicorns or rainbows.

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:26.430
So hopefully one day she'll be making

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:28.050
pasta in the kitchen with me.

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:29.970
- Oh, that's so cool, man.

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:31.050
That's so cool. You're doing this.

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.070
The time you're spending with her,

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:34.140
but also teaching her how to
really cook yourself a meal.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:39.123
I wish I knew how to really
do that, but I can Postmates.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:41.940
Thank you so much for joining us.

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:43.470
This is so cool and it's so beautiful

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:45.990
that you're carrying on
your grandma's legacy.

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:48.660
Everybody pick up Danny's
book, "Danny Loves Pasta"

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:49.860
wherever you get your books.

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:50.820
Thank you so much, Danny.

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:52.839
I'm liking your post right now, all right?

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:54.720
(graphic pings)
(audience applauds)

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:55.920
All right, and that's not all.

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:58.440
Our season-long partner
Pilot, pen makers of G2,

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:00.150
the go-to pen of "The
Kelly Clarkson Show" want

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:02.580
to honor truly unstoppable
people just like you, man,

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:04.170
so they're gonna be writing you a check

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:06.186
for $1,000, how's that sound?

00:03:06.186 --> 00:03:07.613
(audience applauds)
- Thank you, Kelly.

00:03:09.244 --> 00:03:10.077
- Thank you, Danny.

00:03:10.077 --> 00:03:11.640
And thank you to all our guests this hour,

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:13.718
Jennifer Garner, Tony Gonzalez,

00:03:13.718 --> 00:03:15.767
Billie Dean Michelle and Victory.

00:03:15.767 --> 00:03:16.600
Y'all have a great day,

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:18.350
and if it's not, try and change it.

